{"availability":"available","full":"breeznik/agui_demo","name":"agui_demo","description":"AG-UI + LangGraph agent with a plain React and a vanilla JS frontend. No Next.js, no CopilotKit. Streaming, tool calls, shared state, human-in-the-loop interrupts, bring-your-own-key.","category":"Developer tools","language":"JavaScript","stars":18,"forks":3,"created":"2025-11-17T06:34:06Z","updated":"2026-08-19T18:37:22Z","branch":"master","homepage":"","topics":["ag-ui","agentic-ui","agui","ai-agents","aiagents","copilotkit-alternative","fastapi","generative-ui","human-in-the-loop","langchain","langgraph","openrouter","python","react","server-sent-events","streaming","vanilla-javascript"],"demo":"https://docs.ag-ui.com/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T01:25:39.214Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-06T01:25:39.214Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-06T01:25:39.214Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T01:25:39.214Z","stars":18,"forks":3}],"technologies":["React","Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Why this exists: nearly every AG-UI example is Next.js and CopilotKit. If you are on plain React, or on no framework at all, you end up reading someone else's app-router setup to work out which four handlers actually matter. This repo is the same protocol with all of that stripped out, so you can lift the wiring straight into whatever you already have.","A LangGraph ReAct agent talking to a browser: streaming, shared state, tool calls, and human-in-the-loop interrupts. Two frontends that behave identically, React (Vite) and vanilla JS (no framework, no build-time magic), both driven by the same protocol code.","The demo itself is a flight-booking assistant called Breeze. It invents every flight it quotes."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/breeznik/agui_demo/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"ec8c727ac17cac62ed65cb303440eaf3863a6077d63a7a604fc5b1624925e4e3","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T01:25:39.344Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-0